assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when the vendor omits price

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 stopped sending `price` and sends the unit price as `unit_amount` instead. `get_product` only read `p.price ?? null`, so the price came back as null even though the vendor sent one. Both `get_product` and `search_products` now use `price ?? unit_amount`, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output as before. In the recorded call, p-1001's `unit_amount` of 1199 equals its v1 `price`, so it is already in dollars and is passed through without conversion. I haven't seen a 2026-10-01 search response, so the `search_products` change is untested against real data. If a search item has neither field, the price will be missing and output validation will catch it rather than hide it. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass (13 tests).

